{
  "mn5:0.1": "Middle Discourses 5 ",
  "mn5:0.2": "Unblemished ",
  "mn5:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn5:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn5:1.3": "There Sāriputta addressed the mendicants: ",
  "mn5:1.4": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "mn5:1.5": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "mn5:1.6": "Sāriputta said this: ",
  "mn5:2.1": "“Reverends, these four individuals are found in the world. ",
  "mn5:2.2": "What four? ",
  "mn5:2.3": "One individual with a blemish doesn’t truly understand: ‘There is a blemish in me.’ ",
  "mn5:2.4": "But another individual with a blemish does truly understand: ‘There is a blemish in me.’ ",
  "mn5:2.5": "One individual without a blemish doesn’t truly understand: ‘There is no blemish in me.’ ",
  "mn5:2.6": "But another individual without a blemish does truly understand: ‘There is no blemish in me.’ ",
  "mn5:2.7": "In this case, of the two individuals with a blemish, the one who doesn’t understand is said to be worse, ",
  "mn5:2.8": "while the one who does understand is better. ",
  "mn5:2.9": "And of the two individuals without a blemish, the one who doesn’t understand is said to be worse, ",
  "mn5:2.10": "while the one who does understand is better.” ",
  "mn5:3.1": "When he said this, Venerable Mahāmoggallāna said to him: ",
  "mn5:3.2": "“What is the cause, Reverend Sāriputta, what is the reason why, of the two individuals with a blemish, one is s